WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:16.029
Game of Thrones season 9 will definitely happen
in near future

00:00:16.029 --> 00:00:19.509
because not only did the showrunners leave
space for someone to make it,

00:00:19.509 --> 00:00:21.810
but they also left quite a few big clues in
the finale

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.769
that are hinting at huge plot twists for some
of the biggest characters,

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:31.099
like Dany's resurrection, return of many characters,
wars for succession all over Westeros

00:00:31.099 --> 00:00:33.540
and Jon Snow being the new King beyond the
Wall.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.060
Beside that, very well written and executed
season 9 of Game of Thrones

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:40.230
is the only thing that can redeem Game of
Thrones at this point

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.990
because season 8 was so bad and disappointing
that it killed re-watchability of the show

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.719
for so many people.

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:49.950
But if there would be a season 9 and it would
actually be good and answer many unanswered

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:54.170
questions, then season 8 would be nothing
more than a bad season with great previous

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:56.769
seasons
and with a great final season.

00:00:56.769 --> 00:01:00.949
I'm aware that HBO could not do anything,
but oblige with David and Dan's wish to make

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:05.850
only 8 seasons when they actually wanted 10
which was because David and Dan were the ones

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.320
who had the rights to the story's adaptation.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.680
Now when they are done with it, HBO could
and should

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:15.420
and probably will in near future make a sequel
or as I call it season 9 to continue the story

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:18.120
and repair the damage that's been done to
the Game of Thrones.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.860
Thankfully, David and Dan left so much space
for it,

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.890
not having given answers to almost anything
in season 8,

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:28.110
not wrapping up so many stories and leaving
so many clues for what we can expect to happen

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:32.220
with most of our favorite characters as well
as leaving clues to what might happen all

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.920
over Westeros as well.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:38.320
Let's take a look at what we can expect to
happen in the future sequel or season 9,

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:42.430
from Dany's hinted and almost confirmed resurrection
to wars across Westeros,

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:45.600
to all the characters we expected to see in
the season 8

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:50.010
and play a vital role will actually appear
and play their vital role in season 9,

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.270
to White Walker story back in the game, Jon
having yet to fulfill his purpose and the

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.540
Dragon Queen's revenge.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:59.550
Where is Drogon taking killed Dany, was the
question which was answered at the end of

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.640
the finale, and I made a whole video explaining
it right after the show ended which was a

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:06.820
huge hit,
I mean the video, not the ending obviously.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:11.140
In that video, I also explained why Drogon
is taking her to that place and what it means.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:15.171
In the disappointing season 8 finale, Jon
founds himself with no choice, but to kill

00:02:15.171 --> 00:02:20.360
Dany the Mad Queen, influenced by the destruction
of Kings Landing, but also by Tyrion Lannister

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.690
who convinced him that his family will never
be safe as long as Dany lives.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.230
Anyways, Drogon, having a connection with
his mother,

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:30.560
came to the scene and it was a heart-breaking
moment.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.969
Drogon nudges her, tries to wake her, and
it breaks my heart.

00:02:33.969 --> 00:02:37.680
Having destroyed the one thing that made his
mother Daenerys mad and evil,

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:42.510
Drogon gently lifted his mother with his claws
and flew away across the Narrow Sea.

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:46.080
One question remained: Where exactly did Drogon
take Dany?

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:49.189
Sam answered that question in the small council
towards the end of the episode.

00:02:49.189 --> 00:02:53.590
When King Bran asks for an update on the dragon’s
whereabouts late in the finale,

00:02:53.590 --> 00:03:00.650
Sam says “He was last spotted flying east
toward Volantis–” before Bronn cuts him

00:03:00.650 --> 00:03:02.970
off.

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:10.099
What this means is that Dany’s fate is left
up to a debate.

00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:14.549
She’s dead and she might stay that way,
but she might also be resurrected by the Red

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:19.419
Priestess Kinvara who happens to be at the
same city Drogon was last spotted flying towards.

00:03:19.419 --> 00:03:23.319
In fact, I think the showrunners wanted to
imply to us viewers that Dany will probably

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:25.219
not stay dead for long.

00:03:25.219 --> 00:03:27.739
Why else would they mention Drogon flying
toward Volantis?

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:32.040
They could have had Drogon flying toward Valyria,
where Targaryens originate.

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:34.749
This could have been a possible destination
for them both,

00:03:34.749 --> 00:03:38.069
seeing as it's where the Targaryens traditionally
lived with their dragons.

00:03:38.069 --> 00:03:41.440
Second, they could have had Drogon flying
toward the Dothraki Sea.

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:45.499
Drogon and his dragon siblings were born in
Dothraki territory, and they could have had

00:03:45.499 --> 00:03:48.269
him flying back to the place he feels is home.

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:49.269
But they didn’t.

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:52.769
They specifically mentioned Drogon flying
east towards Volantis.

00:03:52.769 --> 00:03:55.269
So why Volantis and what’s in Volantis?

00:03:55.269 --> 00:03:58.200
The first time we see Volantis is in season
5.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:02.019
As Tyrion and Varys were making their way
through a market they spot a Red Priestess

00:04:02.019 --> 00:04:06.819
preaching to a crowd of slaves, who catches
Tyrion's eye as he stops to listen to her

00:04:06.819 --> 00:04:07.819
Sermon.

00:04:07.819 --> 00:04:11.019
She preaches that the Lord of Light has sent
them a savior, the "Dragon Queen" – Daenerys

00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:14.420
Targaryen, who has been WAGING a campaign
against slavery in Meereen.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.870
It’s not just a city where people love and
support Dany, but more importantly, Volantis

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:23.980
is home to Kinvara, a red priestess who made
a brief appearance in season 6 to lend her

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.760
support to the Team Dany.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:29.370
She met Tyrion Lannister and Varys in the
Great Pyramid of Meereen.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.720
Tyrion asked her people to rally behind Daenerys,
to ask them to see her as their protector

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.720
and guardian, not a conqueror.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:38.070
Kinvara was happy to assist Tyrion, saying
Daenerys

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.820
“is the one who was promised.

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.090
From the fire she was reborn to remake the
world...

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:46.440
Daenerys has been sent to lead the people
against the darkness in this war and in the

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.000
Great War still to come.”

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.530
Kinvara promised to spread the word about
Khaleesi throughout Essos.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.920
So we know that the followers of the Lord
of Light stand behind Daenerys,

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:59.340
including Kinvara, who’s titles read: Flame
of Truth, Light of Wisdom, and the First Servant

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:02.510
of the Lord of Light, the High Priestess of
the Red Temple of Volantis.

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:05.970
She's one of the highest-ranking of R'hllor's
clerics.

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:09.860
Since she firmly believes that Daenerys Targaryen
is The Princess That Was Promised,

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:13.860
and the one who will make this world a better
place, much like Melisandre believed in Jon

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:18.920
when she resurrected him, could it be that
Dany will get resurrected by Kinvara?

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.490
In my opinion, it's an obvious yes.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:24.510
If not, they would not mention Drogon flying
toward Volantis which we know is basically

00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:28.940
the capital of the Lord of Light religion,
place filled with Red Priests who worship

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:31.350
Dany
and most importantly that’s where Dany’s

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:36.130
biggest supporter among the Red Priests
and also the most powerful of them all, Kinvara

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.130
is.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:40.300
I think this is the same how they ended Jon’s
story as well.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:43.550
Jon goes back to the Wall and takes the black
even though there’s no need for the Night's

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.090
Watch anymore.

00:05:45.090 --> 00:05:48.850
Jon knows this and tells Tyrion that it’s
ridiculous the order even exists

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:50.360
because there’s no need for them.

00:05:50.360 --> 00:05:54.790
Then in the closing montage, he wears black,
but he also goes beyond the Wall with Tormund,

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.310
Ghost and a bunch of wildlings.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:00.760
Yes, Jon is wearing black, much like Dany
is dead, but it’s implied that he’s not

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.600
coming back to the Wall,
but is rather staying beyond, just like how

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.320
it’s implied Dany will not stay dead for
long

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.640
because the place Drogon is taking her to,
Volantis, pretty much means Dany will get

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.890
resurrected.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.150
Jon becomes King beyond the Wall and Dany
the Queen of Essos.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:18.010
That's an ideal start of season 9.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:23.780
Dany's storyline would be about her resurrection,
her realization that Essos is where she belongs,

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.790
but also her seeking revenge for those who
wronged her.

00:06:26.790 --> 00:06:31.000
After being resurrected, Dany with Drogon
and Kinvara by her side would go from Volantis

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.840
to Mereen where she left Daario and the Second
Sons in charge.

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:37.890
Dany will decide to rule lands in Essos where
people love her

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.790
instead of Westeros where she's feared and
hated.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:44.890
Same as Jon when Jon was resurrected, Dany
will not want to rule something where people

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:49.910
don’t appreciate her and love her, she will
rule Essos instead, where she is their MHYSSA.

00:06:49.910 --> 00:06:52.840
Her ultimate goal is to be the Queen of Essos
based in Mereen

00:06:52.840 --> 00:06:57.320
because those are people who deserve her,
but before that she will seek revenge.

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.690
As I said, Jon Snow did avenge his own death
upon being resurrected as well.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:05.840
Dany's list includes Jon who killed her, Tyrion
who made Jon do it

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.240
and Sansa who pretty much started all of it
by revealing Jon has the best claims to Tyrion

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.770
who then told it to Varys and that's when
the whole plot against her started.

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:18.620
Sansa was Littlefinger's student, she knew
this would cause Dany's downfall and Dany

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:43.320
herself recognized that as well in episode
5 of season 8.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:48.030
She will go to Westeros with Drogon, Kinvara,
Daario and his 2 000 Second Sons, as well

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:52.810
as remained Unsullied and Dothraki to seek
revenge against those who plotted and executed

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.550
her, just like Jon did after he was resurrected.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:08:00.860
The Unsullied numbering 4 000 heavy infantry
at the end of season 8 left for Naath,

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:04.720
but I'm certain they will go back to Dany
upon finding out she's alive again.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:09.340
The Dothraki numbering 50 000 light cavalry,
according to the official report, left Kings

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:13.750
Landing for Essos and will also without a
doubt continue to serve their Khaleesi when

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:16.230
they find out she's not dead after all.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:21.060
And just like that, Dany again has the greatest
army numbering 56 000 and Drogon,

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.470
along with her advisors Kinvara, Grey Worm,
and Daario.

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:29.330
In season 9 I would imagine Dany is driven
by revenge, less naive, and more calculated.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:34.120
Basically, she will go against half of the
Kingdom; the North ruled by Sansa,

00:08:34.120 --> 00:08:38.370
the Westerlands ruled by Tyrion, but also
against Riverlands and the Vale who will support

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.080
the North
as they are Stark's relatives.

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:46.360
The Crownlands will also support them as Bran
Stark rules it now and he will help his sister.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:49.510
The Reach that is now ruled by Bronn would
also support them

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:52.460
since its Tyrion and Bran who gave him those
lands and titles,

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:55.440
but I doubt Bronn will be lord paramount of
the Reach for long.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:59.230
There is no way all the proud houses of the
Reach would be okay with some random sellsword

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:02.220
with no noble blood or claim to the Reach
be their lord.

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:06.740
Bronn would 100% end up dead in a ditch as
soon as he showed up to claim Highgarden,

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:11.120
then the Hightowers or Redwynes would declare
themselves either lords of Highgarden

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:13.830
or even Kings of the Reach and make it independent.

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:16.279
Dorne and the Iron Islands would then follow
as well.

00:09:16.279 --> 00:09:19.430
But even if all these kingdoms don't declare
independency,

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:23.920
that still doesn't change the fact that both
the Iron Islands ruled by Yara Greyjoy

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:28.680
and Dorne ruled by the new Prince of Dorne
would definitely pledge their support Dany

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.840
when they find out she's been resurrected.

00:09:30.840 --> 00:09:34.620
In the season 8 episode 4, Prince of Dorne
pledged himself to Dany

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:36.870
and I believe he would honor that pledge.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:40.140
If not, Dany can always win his support by
marrying him,

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.930
as we all know that's the best way to make
allies.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:45.790
Two kingdoms are left to declare their support
to.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.370
King beyond the Wall, Jon Snow is an obvious
one,

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:53.060
Dany is coming to kill him as well, so he
joins forces with Sansa and Bran Stark.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:57.880
It would also be nice for season 9 to show
why Jon's true parentage was a big thing,

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:00.510
except for being a plot to make Dany paranoid.

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:04.060
Giving it some importance, as well as showing
us what was the reason Jon was brought back

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:07.020
to life because he's not fulfilled his purpose
yet.

00:10:07.020 --> 00:10:09.830
Beric Dondarrion did and died in the process.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:14.100
Melisandre fulfilled her purpose as well,
didn't die in the process, but died when it

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:15.100
was done.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:19.611
Jon Snow didn't die, he's still alive, meaning
he still has a role to play, a purpose to

00:10:19.611 --> 00:10:20.611
fulfill.

00:10:20.611 --> 00:10:21.611
That's something I'm looking for in the future
Game of Thrones sequel.

00:10:21.611 --> 00:10:23.180
Stormlands and its Lord Gendry is a complicated
one.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:27.700
Yes, he's a good friend of Starks and Jon
Snow, but they are not the one who legitimized

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:30.850
him,
gave him those lands and titles, it was Dany

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.640
and I believe his honor will bound him to
help Dany.

00:10:33.640 --> 00:10:38.660
After all, Tyrion did tell Dany that “Lord
of Storms End who will be forever loyal to

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:39.660
you.''

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:51.000
after she legitimized him.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:54.010
Although Dany is coming to avenge her death,
as I said earlier,

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:56.300
she doesn't plan on ruling Westeros.

00:10:56.300 --> 00:10:58.750
That's a good parallel with Roberts Rebellion.

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:02.680
In both cases, the Throne wasn't the main
goal, but at the end when the vengence is

00:11:02.680 --> 00:11:04.480
over,
someone has to rule it.

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.980
I think that's when Gendry comes in for Dany.

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:11.340
She doesn't want to rule Westeros, she just
wants revenge, but someone will have to rule

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:14.240
it when the war is won and that's when Gendry
comes in.

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:18.200
To secure his loyalty, I believe she will
promise Gendry the throne.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:20.870
Melisandre did prophesied that Gendry will
make Kings rise and fall.

00:11:20.870 --> 00:11:25.779
We didn't see him making kings rise and fall
in season 8, perhaps we will in season 9.

00:11:25.779 --> 00:11:29.750
We all know how accurate Melisandre's prophecies
turned out to be in the end.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.670
All of this makes for the bloodiest war in
Westeros.

00:11:32.670 --> 00:11:36.690
The argument that Bran Stark, this powerful
three-eyed raven could stop any of this happening

00:11:36.690 --> 00:11:40.970
before it actually happens, falls in water,
because if he was that powerful,

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:43.770
then he would stop the Night King before he
actually happened.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:46.310
Bran couldn't even warg into the Night King's
dragon,

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.960
so there will not be any use of him when Daenerys
comes back.

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:52.220
He lives in the past.

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.960
In season 9 we could also see many important
events that we were promised to see in Game

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:57.060
of Thrones but didn't.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:01.030
We could finally see Bran's visions of the
past of Robert's Rebellion,

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:05.800
Robert vs Rhaegar, as well as Rhaegar Targaryen's
reasons to run away with Lyanna Stark

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.480
without saying a word to anyone.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:11.170
What was the reason behind them two not telling
everyone they're in love,

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:15.270
but instead, Rhaegar made it seem like he
kidnapped Lyanna and started a war

00:12:15.270 --> 00:12:17.460
that would destroy the Targaryen dynasty.

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:21.029
Perhaps we could also find out more about
the White Walkers and the Night King as well,

00:12:21.029 --> 00:12:24.200
something Bran is surely eager to find out
himself.

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:28.720
As he said it himself, Bran Stark lives mostly
in the past now, spending much of his time

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:32.010
in greensight,
so getting to see some of the mysteries unravel

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:34.380
is always a good choice.

00:12:34.380 --> 00:12:37.920
Perhaps season 9 would also bring the White
Walkers back into the fold with the Nights

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:38.920
Queen.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:42.870
We know that the Night King was killed and
destroyed in season 8 along with the White

00:12:42.870 --> 00:12:46.210
Walkers he created and the wights he and his
lieutenants created,

00:12:46.210 --> 00:12:50.160
but that doesn't mean we've seen the end of
the White Walker story.

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:54.140
Season 9 could introduce us with far more
powerful and complex character than the Night

00:12:54.140 --> 00:12:55.390
King,
the Nights Queen.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:59.290
There are many other parts of the story that
season 9 would include as well,

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.720
such as Arya Stark's adventures.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.950
I would expect the return of Jaqen and especially
the return of Quaithe

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.750
who I believe Dany will meet after she's resurrected.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:12.210
All in all, season 8 left a lot of space for
season 9 or some kind of a sequel to Game

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.130
of Thrones
with all the clues it left behind and especially

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:20.270
with a confirmation that Drogon is taking
Dany to Volantis where Kinvara is, Dany's

00:13:20.270 --> 00:13:23.510
supporter and the most powerful follower of
the Lord of Light,

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:26.880
far more powerful than Melisandre who brought
Jon back.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:29.000
Why else would Drogon be flying to Volantis?

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.839
That’s not where they were born,
that’s not their ancestral home, that’s

00:13:32.839 --> 00:13:34.150
not where they lived.

00:13:34.150 --> 00:13:38.040
The only connection Dany has with that place
is the Red Priest who supports her

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:40.850
and who has the ability to resurrect people.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:45.060
All the characters we expected to see in season
8 and play the vital role we could see in

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:46.430
season 9.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:49.480
Everything left unexplained could be explained,
and most importantly,

00:13:49.480 --> 00:13:52.990
we could get a satisfying ending to the series
we all fell in love with.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:56.380
We definitely will not get season 9 anytime
soon,

00:13:56.380 --> 00:14:00.220
but I believe we’ll get some kind of a sequel
to repair the damage done to both Game of

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:02.310
Thrones and HBO.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:05.940
Perhaps the trilogy, but something will definitely
follow up on where season 8 left.

